Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-05-2000||12:45 PM||||Ok, this is a street race that took place 3 nights ago. I decided not to post before because I figured nobody would believe it.  Anyhow, if you don't agree with street racing, please don't read this!  It took place at 2am with no cars in from or behind us.  Another Fiero guy and I were just driving my new Fiero to his shop across town.  Before I tell you what we raced, keep in mind that this was 1FST2M6's car, and he clocked 0-60 in 5.2 on the dyno with the addition of the 4.10 gearing.  So anyhow....  I see some headlights in my side-view mirror coming up fast.  At that very second, the light at the intersection a few yards ahead of us turn from yellow to red.  A couple of punks in a red 98 or 99 Z28 pull up beside us.  And yes, it was a Z28(LS1.)  It had the Z28 badges, SLP exhaust, and of course that V8 rumble.  I THINK it was an auto.  I say: "I think we're going to lose..."  My friend says, "This car launches pretty car, I don't know...)  Meanwhile, the idiots in daddys Z28 are revving the living crap out of it.  So I quickly glance around for cops and peds, give them a nod, and rev it up a bit.  Light turns green.  I launced it at 2000 rpm.  The LS1 screeched them a bit and mine just made a loud chirp and we took off.  We pulled a whole car-length on him through the light! I shifted to second and he started gaining fast.  By the time I was ready for third gear, he had a couple car lengths on me so I back off.  We gave each other the thumbs up afterwords though. I was pretty impressed.  A few minutes later we were pull over for having Georgia plates that were unrecognized.  The cop was really nice though, he just had to call in to have them look up the plates and let us go.  Funny thing, the cop said his friend had an '86 INDY GT.   Hehe... yeah right. I didn't argue with him though.  After we started back home, my friend got a call on his cell phone from someone.  Apparently, the guys in the LS1 called a mutual friend(who also drives nothing but Fiero's) of Brad(my friend) and were wondering if they knew of a gold Fiero.  Then someone ELSE called Brad and said they heard of a street racing involving a Red Camaro and another car on the police scanner.  Guess we lucked-out.  Anyhow, that's all for now folks.<P>------------------<BR>Gold 86 SE V6 4-sp w/4.10 gears, Eibach springs, Koni's all around w/some poly bushings<BR>Yoko's<BR>Coated headers<BR>ACT 4-puck clutch<BR>MSD ignition<BR>Flowmaster w/ mandrel bent 2.5 pipe<BR>extrude honed intake<BR>Lots of fuel system mods... etc etc...||||reg||4
